Subject: Tech:  Price of Macs vs. PCs

/hawk writes:
> Macs are now priced on Par with Top tier IBM Clones

Also remember Macs come with many options that might cost extra on a PC:

- mouse, you don't need to buy a mouse, card, driver.
- i/o ports built in, you don't need to buy an i/o card.
- 4-channel stereo sound driver, you don't need to buy a sound card.
- high resolution graphics capability, you don't need to buy a graphics 
card.
- GUI OS, you don't need to buy DOS and Windows NT.
- printer port, you don't need a card, driver.
- low-level networking for home use, you don't need network cards.
- server/client disk sharing, you don't need to buy server/client software.
- conversion for Apple, Mac, DOS diskettes, you don't need special hardware 
or software to trade diskettes with other OS's

Also compare Consumer Reports, and weekly computer magazines for support 
costs.  Macs cost much less than PC's to support.  Less training, less 
internal conflicts between programs, less hardware configuration, more 
automatic configuration, and less general failures than PCs.
